{"title":"Career roadmap · Design Consultant","role":"Design Consultant","summary":"A Design Consultant in the interior-design field advises clients on space planning, aesthetics, materials, furniture, lighting, colour, functionality, budget, and overall design direction for residential, commercial, hospitality, retail, workplace, healthcare, and other interior environments.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Design Consultant in the interior-design field advises clients on space planning, aesthetics, materials, furniture, lighting, colour, functionality, budget, and overall design direction for residential, commercial, hospitality, retail, workplace, healthcare, and other interior environments."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Des in Interior Design provides the core design foundation. To become a strong consultant, students should additionally develop client consultation, spatial planning, technical drawings, materials knowledge, budgeting, project coordination, 3D visualisation, building-services awareness, sustainability, and business development."},{"type":"note","label":"Important distinction","text":"A Design Consultant may lead design recommendations and client decisions, but structural, electrical, fire-safety, architectural, or other regulated technical work must be handled by appropriately qualified professionals where required."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Interior Design Intern, Design Assistant, Junior Interior Designer"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Interior Designer, Design Consultant, Interior Design Consultant"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Senior Interior Designer, Senior Design Consultant"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Lead Designer, Design Manager, Project Design Lead"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},