ity Designer"},{"text":"Residential Designer"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lead Interior Designer"},{"text":"Lead Design Consultant"},{"text":"Design Manager"},{"text":"Project Design Manager"},{"text":"Design Lead"},{"text":"Senior Design Strategist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Leadership"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Director"},{"text":"Head of Interior Design"},{"text":"Creative Director"},{"text":"Design Consultancy Director"},{"text":"Studio Principal"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Independent"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interior Design Consultant"},{"text":"Interior Design Studio Founder"},{"text":"Design Consultant"},{"text":"Interior Design Entrepreneur"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What Employers May Test"},{"type":"h","text":"Client brief"},{"type":"p","text":"A client has a 2BHK apartment, a limited budget and needs a home office. How would you approach the project?"},{"type":"p","text":"Expected process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Client Needs","Site Study","Space Planning","Priorities","Budget","Concept","Materials","Design","Implementation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Space planning"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you improve circulation in a small apartment?"},{"type":"p","text":"Consider:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Furniture dimensions"},{"text":"Circulation paths"},{"text":"Storage"},{"text":"Multi-functional furniture"},{"text":"Zoning"},{"text":"Natural light"},{"text":"Visual openness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Budget"},{"type":"p","text":"The client's preferred materials exceed the budget by 25%. What would you do?"},{"type":"p","text":"Consider:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prioritisation"},{"text":"Alternative materials"},{"text":"Value engineering"},{"text":"Supplier comparison"},{"text":"Reuse"},{"text":"Custom vs ready-made furniture"},{"text":"Phased implementation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Client conflict"},{"type":"p","text":"The client rejects your design after several weeks of work."},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Requirement clarification"},{"text":"Design rationale"},{"text":"Alternative concepts"},{"text":"Scope management"},{"text":"Professional communication"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A master's is not mandatory for becoming a design consultant, but can support specialisation and leadership."},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Des Interior Design"},{"text":"M.Des Spatial Design"},{"text":"M.Des Furniture Design"},{"text":"M.Des Exhibition Design"},{"text":"M.Des Environmental Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Related"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architecture/Interior-related programmes where eligibility permits"},{"text":"Design Management"},{"text":"Sustainable Design"},{"text":"Lighting Design"},{"text":"Building/Construction Management"},{"text":"Real Estate/Facilities Management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"BIM"},{"text":"Environmental Design"},{"text":"Sustainable Architecture/Design"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Experience Design"}]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant master's programmes include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interior Design"},{"text":"Interior Architecture"},{"text":"Spatial Design"},{"text":"Environmental Design"},{"text":"Exhibition Design"},{"text":"Sustainable Design"},{"text":"Furniture Design"},{"text":"Hospitality Design"},{"text":"Retail Design"},{"text":"Workplace Design"},{"text":"Design Management"},{"text":"Lighting Design"},{"text":"Experience Design"},{"text":"Architectural Technology"},{"text":"BIM"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Programme titles and professional recognition vary by country, so applicants should verify whether a programme is intended for interior design practice, interior architecture, or design research."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"0–2 years"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Intern → Junior Interior Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"3D"},{"text":"Drawings"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Site work"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 years"},{"type":"h","text":"Interior Designer → Design Consultant"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Client handling"},{"text":"Design development"},{"text":"Budgets"},{"text":"Vendors"},{"text":"Complete projects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 years"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Designer → Senior Design Consultant / Design Lead"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Major projects"},{"text":"Client strategy"},{"text":"Team leadership"},{"text":"Design direction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"8–12+ years"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Manager → Design Director / Studio Principal"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Business"},{"text":"Design strategy"},{"text":"Major clients"},{"text":"Team building"},{"text":"Studio growth"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Career Evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Interior design consultancy will increasingly combine spatial design with AI, BIM, digital twins, smart buildings, sustainability, and data-driven user experience."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI Interior Design Consultant"},{"text":"Smart Interior Designer"},{"text":"Digital Twin Interior Specialist"},{"text":"Computational Interior Designer"},{"text":"Sustainable Design Consultant"},{"text":"Workplace Experience Strategist"},{"text":"Spatial Data Designer"},{"text":"Smart Building Experience Designer"},{"text":"Generative Interior Design Specialist"},{"text":"Immersive Spatial Experience Designer"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI applications"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Concept generation"},{"text":"Layout alternatives"},{"text":"Material recommendations"},{"text":"Style exploration"},{"text":"Space optimisation"},{"text":"Cost estimation support"},{"text":"Client preference analysis"},{"text":"Rendering"},{"text":"VR environments"},{"text":"Energy/design scenario analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The designer remains responsible for client interpretation, spatial judgement, technical coordination, aesthetics, safety awareness, material selection, feasibility, and final design decisions."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"flow","items":["Space Planning","Concept Design","Colour","Materials","Furniture","Lighting"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"flow","items":["AutoCAD","SketchUp","Revit/BIM","3D Rendering","Technical Documentation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"flow","items":["BOQ","Estimation","Procurement","Vendor Management","Site Coordination"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Client"},{"type":"flow","items":["Briefing","Presentation","Negotiation","Proposal Writing","Relationship Management"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Business"},{"type":"flow","items":["Pricing","Design Fees","Business Development","Sales","Portfolio Marketing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainability"},{"type":"flow","items":["Green Materials","Circular Design","Biophilic Design","Energy Awareness"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Future"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI","Generative Design","BIM","Digital Twins","VR/AR","Smart Interiors"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Des Interior Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Interior Design Intern"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Interior Designer / Design Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Interior Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Consultant"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Design Consultant / Design Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Director / Head of Interior Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Studio Principal / Independent Design Consultant"},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Interior Design","strong spatial-design fundamentals","CAD/BIM","3D visualisation","materials","technical documentation","project management","client consulting","site experience","AI/digital design skills is the strongest pathway."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The portfolio should contain 6–8 substantial projects, including at least one residential, commercial/workplace, hospitality or retail, sustainable, and technology-enabled interior project."},{"type":"p","text":"Each case study should demonstrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Client Brief","Site Analysis","User Needs","Concept","Space Planning","Materials","Furniture & Lighting","Technical Drawings","3D Visualisation","Budget","Execution Strategy"]},{"type":"p","text":"For a Design Consultant, the portfolio should prove not only that the graduate can create attractive spaces, but that they can understand a client's problem, develop a practical design within constraints, communicate the proposal clearly, and take the project toward implementation."}]}]}